{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"id\":7982165,\"site\":\"lawnsguide\",\"type\":\"landscaping\",\"short_title\":\"design-low-maintenance-front-yard-ideas\",\"language\":\"en\",\"published_time\":\"2026-08-08 18:12:22\",\"modified_time\":\"2026-08-08 18:12:22\",\"author\":\"Lisa Thompson\",\"img\":null,\"title\":\"How to Design a Low-Maintenance Front Yard\",\"description\":\"Design a beautiful low-maintenance front yard with hydrozoning, evergreen structure, and smart plant choices.\",\"url\":null,\"body\":\"<h2>The Case for Low-Maintenance Landscaping</h2><p>A well-designed low-maintenance front yard saves hours of weekly work while still looking polished and welcoming. The key is choosing the right plants and hardscaping from the start.</p><h2>Core Design Principles</h2><h3>Reduce Lawn Area</h3><p>Replace turf grass with mulched beds, groundcovers, or hardscaping. Every square foot of lawn you eliminate saves 30-45 minutes of weekly maintenance during growing season.</p><h3>Group Plants by Water Needs</h3><p>Hydrozoning — grouping plants with similar water requirements — simplifies irrigation and prevents over or under-watering. Drought-tolerant plants near the street, moisture-loving plants near downspouts.</p><h3>Use Evergreen Structure</h3><p>Build your design around evergreen shrubs and small trees that provide year-round structure. Add perennials and annuals for seasonal color pops that require minimal upkeep.</p><h2>Top Low-Maintenance Plants</h2><ul><li><strong>Ornamental grasses</strong> — cut back once a year in late winter</li><li><strong>Sedum</strong> — drought-proof, blooms late season</li><li><strong>Boxwood</strong> — needs trimming 1-2 times per year</li><li><strong>Hostas</strong> — thrive in shade, zero maintenance</li></ul>\",\"tag\":null,\"is_online\":\"Y\",\"subtype\":null,\"slug\":null,\"cover_image\":null,\"status\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-08-08 18:12:22\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":3600,"tags":[]}